(Slide 20: Grammar Skills) Tj
T*
(Slide 21: Grammar 1: There is / There are ? | We use "There is" and "There are" to say that) Tj
T*
(something exists in a place. | Singular (One thing) | Use There is (There's) | Positive (+):) Tj
T*
("There is a big bed in my room." | Negative (-): "There isn't a TV in the kitchen." | Plural) Tj
T*
((Two or more things) | Use There are | Positive (+): "There are two armchairs in the living) Tj
T*
(room." | Negative (-): "There aren't any books on the bookshelf.") Tj
T*
(Slide 22: Grammar 2: Asking Questions ? | How to ask about things in a house! | Singular) Tj
T*
(Question | Question: "Is there a fridge in the kitchen?" | Answer: "Yes, there is." / "No,) Tj
T*
(there isn't." | Plural Question | Question: "Are there any rugs in the living room?" | Answer:) Tj
T*
("Yes, there are." / "No, there aren't.") Tj
T*
(Slide 23: Grammar 3: Make Longer Sentences! ? | Don't speak like a robot! Connect your short) Tj
T*
(sentences with linking words. | AND (+) | Addition | "There is a bed and a wardrobe in my) Tj
T*
(room." | BUT (+/-) | Contrast | "There is a sofa, but there isn't an armchair." | OR | Choices) Tj
T*
(/ Negative | "Is there a bath or a shower?" | BECAUSE | Reason - Why? | "I love my bedroom) Tj
T*
(because it is very quiet.") Tj
T*
(Slide 24: Let's Practice | Click here) Tj
T*
(Slide 25: Speaking Like a Native! ?? | Read this paragraph. See how the words connect! | "In) Tj
T*
(my living room, there is a big sofa and a smart TV. There are two small tables, but there) Tj
T*
(isn't a rug. I like this room because it is very bright and comfortable. What about you? Is) Tj
T*
(there a TV or a bookshelf in your living room?") Tj
T*
(Slide 26: The Dream House! ? | Speaking Activity - | Work with a partner. Take turns designing) Tj
T*
(your dream home! | 01 | Student A: Ask Questions | Find out what is in Student B's dream room.) Tj
